# SBOM Comparison Report

**mikebom v0.1.0-alpha.47** vs **syft v1.42.3**

Formats: **mikebom v0.1.0-alpha.47** = `spdx-json`, **syft v1.42.3** = `spdx-json`.

Methodology inspired by [mlieberman85's SBOM quality benchmark](https://gist.github.com/mlieberman85/cb0ed7b600efb211dce0633e2c392626).

---

## Key Insight: Source SBOM vs Binary SBOM

mikebom v0.1.0-alpha.47 describes SOURCE (e.g. go.sum/module graph) while syft v1.42.3 describes a BUILT BINARY. A source SBOM lists the full transitive/test dependency set; a binary SBOM lists only what is compiled in. This explains most package-count and coverage differences below.

